35,2,1,talk,Minako,,The timing confirms my fear: over two hours per pass. The inconsistent standards make it worse. We need a fixed definition.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, The data is damning. Two people cook, three make coffee, yet the burden is equal. We must weight the work by actual usage, not just presence.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"@Minako, two hours is scary! And the grout gets black again in eleven days because the window is tiny. We need a better plan!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, two hours is a lot. I found the spray costs 2,300 yen monthly, often bought twice. We must track who pays.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Minako, the previous tenants divided rooms permanently and stopped speaking by year two. We must avoid that silence.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, weighting by usage is logical, but the two-hour block is the real bottleneck. I need to know if we can split that time to protect my schedule.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, Splitting the time is sensible, but only if the tasks are defined. We cannot slice a vague two-hour block into fairer pieces.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Benjamin, I agree! If we split the two hours, I can handle the grout before it turns black again. It feels much more doable!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I agree. But the 2,300 yen in supplies is a separate worry. I need to know if the management office can bill us directly to avoid confusion.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Shizue, tracking the money is wise, but the previous tenants’ silence was born from rigid division. Let us ensure our system invites conversation, not just compliance.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Sakura, splitting the block is key. If I handle the kitchen, you take the bathroom, we avoid the two-hour pileup.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, I support splitting the block, but we must weight the kitchen share. Two cooks cannot pay the same as three coffee drinkers.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Minako, I love that! If I just do the bathroom, I can check the grout every few days. No more guessing if it’s ready!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, splitting the time helps, but I worry about the 4,200 yen hourly rate if we hire help. I need to see how that compares to our current costs.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
